<h3>My Variables</h3>
<p id="a631de6b-7ec5-4bc0-a120-1d24205ecc0b" class=""><strong>Exercise:</strong> Create a new variable named <code>todayDate</code> and set it
    today's date. </p>

    <p><strong>Answer</strong>: </p>

    <!--- Declare and initialize variable todayDate --->
    <bx:set todayDate=#now()#>
    The todayDate variable: <bx:output>#todayDate#</bx:output><br />
    Is todayDate a date type of variable? <bx:output>#isValid("date",todayDate)#</bx:output>

    <hr/>

    <p id="b0b17cfe-e668-4793-b3e9-00e27a9325fa" class=""><strong>Exercise</strong>: Format the output for todayDate to be more 
        human-readable version of the todayDate variable BUT don&#x27;t change the underlying variable.</p>

    <p><strong>Answer</strong>: using short mask with DateFormat()</p>

    <!--- using short mask with DateFormat() --->
    Formatted todayDate: <bx:output>#DateFormat(date=todayDate, mask="short")#</bx:output>


<hr/>

    <p id="fdd75171-c4ef-49e8-af90-0149b2170f0f" class=""><strong>Exercise</strong>: Below, add up the price of your 5 books in
        your Excel Project. Can you do it with only one variable name? Let&#x27;s call it <code>totalBookCost</code>. Hint: Start
        with <code>&lt;bx:set totalBookCost=0&gt;</code> and go from there. Think you can do it? Don&#x27;t forget to output the
        final amount to the page.</p>   

    <p><strong>Answer</strong>: using compound add assignment operator for each book</p>

    <!--- declare and initialize variable totalBookCost --->
    <bx:set totalBookCost = 0>
    <!--- add cost of bookOne using compound add assignment operator --->
    <bx:set totalBookCost += 19.99>
    <!--- add cost of bookTwo using compound add assignment operator --->
    <bx:set totalBookCost += 19.99>
    <!--- add cost of bookThree using compound add assignment operator --->
    <bx:set totalBookCost += 52.95>
    <!--- add cost of bookFour using compound add assignment operator --->
    <bx:set totalBookCost += 27.50>
    <!--- add cost of bookFive using compound add assignment operator --->
    <bx:set totalBookCost += 29.95>
    
    <!--- https://boxlang.ortusbooks.com/boxlang-language/reference/built-in-functions/format/numberformat --->
    <!--- using mask for dollar currency with NumberFormat() --->
    <bx:output>The total book cost for five books: 
    #NumberFormat(number=totalBookCost, mask="_$,9.99")#</bx:output>